---
import LayoutBase from "../layouts/LayoutBase.astro";
---

<LayoutBase pageTitle="About me" pageDescription="Get to know Marcio Morgado.">
    <section
        id="hero"
        aria-label="Hero"
        class="relative w-screen h-fit md:h-screen flex flex-col py-10 px-6 lg:py-[60px] lg:px-14 justify-center text-2xl md:text-3xl lg:text-4xl xl:text-[56px] xl:leading-normal before:content-[''] before:absolute before:-z-10 before:inset-0 before:opacity-[0.4] before:bg-[url('/about_me.svg')] before:bg-origin-border before:bg-contain before:bg-repeat-y">
        <h1 class="text-UtOrange font-semibold">Meet the designer</h1>
        <p class="text-Charcoal font-light lg:w-[40ch]">
            I’m a designer who’s done it all — from shaping visual identities to solving complex product challenges.
            Thirteen years, three roles, one goal: create experiences people enjoy using.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section
        data-analytics-section="designing-with-purpose"
        class="relative py-6 px-6 text-Charcoal grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-6 lg:py-[60px] lg:px-14">
        <div class="col-span-2">
            <h2 class="max-w-[250px] text-lg md:text-3xl text-UtOrange">Designing with purpose</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="lg:w-[70ch] md:col-start-3 md:-col-end-1 xl:text-lg">
            <p class="mb-4">
                I design with one thing in mind: making the complex feel simple. With a strong eye for detail and a deep
                appreciation for usability, I focus on creating products that are clear, intuitive, and — hopefully —
                delightful to use.
            </p>
            <p>
                Whether I’m wireframing a new feature or refining micro-interactions, I love those small decisions that
                make an experience feel just right. And since great design is never really finished, I’m always
                learning, testing, and iterating to make every version better than the last.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section
        data-analytics-section="beyond-the-screen"
        class="relative py-6 px-6 text-Charcoal grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-6 lg:py-[60px] lg:px-14">
        <div class="col-span-2">
            <h2 class="max-w-[250px] text-lg md:text-3xl text-UtOrange">Beyond the screen</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="lg:w-[70ch] md:col-start-3 md:-col-end-1 xl:text-lg">
            <p class="mb-4">
                When I’m not designing, you’ll usually find me riding my motorcycle, exploring new video games, or
                spending time with my family. I’ve got a natural curiosity about how things work, and I live by the idea
                that “knowledge doesn’t take up space” — you never know when something random will spark a great
                solution.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section
        data-analytics-section="how-i-work"
        class="relative py-6 px-6 text-Charcoal grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-6 lg:py-[60px] lg:px-14">
        <div class="col-span-2">
            <h2 class="max-w-[250px] text-lg md:text-3xl text-UtOrange">How I work</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="lg:w-[70ch] md:col-start-3 md:-col-end-1 xl:text-lg">
            <p class="mb-4">
                To me, design is about bringing order to chaos. Big, messy problems don’t scare me — I break them down
                into small, manageable questions and solve them one at a time.
            </p>
            <p>
                I start with research and rough sketches, collaborate early with engineers to catch potential pitfalls,
                and iterate until the solution is both usable and buildable. My mantra? Great design is invisible. If
                users get their job done without noticing the design, I’ve succeeded.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section
        data-analytics-section="resume"
        class="relative py-6 px-6 text-Charcoal grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-6 lg:py-[60px] lg:px-14">
        <div class="col-span-2">
            <h2 class="max-w-[250px] text-lg md:text-3xl text-UtOrange">Resume</h2>
            <a href="#" class="text-sm underline">Download the PDF [128kb]</a>
        </div>

        <div class="lg:w-[70ch] md:col-start-3 md:-col-end-1 space-y-8">
            <section class="space-y-4">
                <h3 class="uppercase font-semibold">Experience</h3>
                <div class="space-y-8">
                    <!-- Work entry -->
                    <div>
                        <p>
                            <span class="font-semibold">Senior Product Designer,</span> Nasdaq
                        </p>
                        <p class="mb-2">Jan 2021 — April 2025</p>
                        <ul class="list-disc space-y-2">
                            <li>
                                Owned multiple design initiatives across Nasdaq Data Link, delivering polished,
                                high-impact product experiences for institutional users and data consumers.
                            </li>

                            <li>
                                Led the end-to-end design of Data Link Manager, a tool for configuring complex dataset
                                access across global financial clients. Shipped improvements that reduced onboarding
                                friction and enhanced trust in entitlement management.
                            </li>

                            <li>
                                Drove user journey mapping, wireframes, prototypes, and high-fidelity UI for core
                                features—collaborating daily with product, engineering, compliance, and customer success
                                teams.
                            </li>

                            <li>
                                Used Figma, Miro, and prototyping tools to rapidly explore concepts, organize
                                documentation, and present design direction to stakeholders across the org.
                            </li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                        <p>
                            <span class="font-semibold">Marketing / Product Designer,</span> Quandl Inc.
                        </p>
                        <p class="mb-2">May 2019 — Jan 2021</p>
                        <ul class="list-disc space-y-2">
                            <li>
                                Played a key role in rebranding and replatforming Quandl to Nasdaq Data Link, defining
                                new interaction patterns and content architecture for the productʼs public-facing
                                interface.
                            </li>

                            <li>
                                Worked cross-functionally on core features like dataset search, product comparison, and
                                onboarding flows—building journey maps and conducting usability sessions to shape
                                direction.
                            </li>

                            <li>
                                Partnered with product and engineering to scope and deliver incremental improvements to
                                internal-facing tooling used by sales and support teams.
                            </li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                        <p>
                            <span class="font-semibold">Designer,</span> HM&E Design
                        </p>
                        <p class="mb-2">Sept 2012 – Feb 2019</p>
                        <ul class="list-disc space-y-2">
                            <li>
                                Led projects from concept to release, translating client briefs into print and digital
                                deliverables.
                            </li>

                            <li>
                                Presented creative concepts directly to clients and supported request-for-proposal
                                responses.
                            </li>

                            <li>
                                Provided on-set art direction and implemented client brand systems across new
                                collateral.
                            </li>

                            <li>Iterated on designs based on feedback from clients and the creative director.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>
            <div class="flex flex-col gap-6 md:flex-row justify-between">
                <section>
                    <div>
                        <h3 class="uppercase font-semibold">Skills</h3>
                        <ul class="space-y-2">
                            <li>UI/UX Design</li>
                            <li>Design Systems Prototyping</li>
                            <li>Responsive Design</li>
                            <li>User Research & Testing</li>
                            <li>Information Architecture</li>
                            <li>Accessibility</li>
                            <li>Design Documentation</li>
                            <li>Branding & Identity</li>
                            <li>Visual Design</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <section>
                    <h3 class="uppercase font-semibold">Tools</h3>
                    <ul class="space-y-2">
                        <li>Figma</li>
                        <li>Sketch</li>
                        <li>Adobe CC</li>
                        <li>Zeplin</li>
                        <li>Asana</li>
                        <li>Webflow</li>
                        <li>Framer</li>
                    </ul>
                </section>

                <section>
                    <h3 class="uppercase font-semibold">Development</h3>
                    <ul class="space-y-2">
                        <li>HTML/CSS</li>
                        <li>JavaScript / jQuery</li>
                        <li>Tailwind / Sass</li>
                        <li>GitHub</li>
                        <li>Zeplin / Figma Dev Mode</li>
                        <li>Jira</li>
                    </ul>
                </section>
            </div>

            <section>
                <h3 class="uppercase font-semibold">Education</h3>
                <ul class="space-y-2">
                    <li>
                        <span class="font-semibold">Graphic Design Advanced Diploma</span>
                        <br />Humber College
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <span class="font-semibold">WCAG 2.0 Certificate </span><br />Eliquo Training & Development
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </section>
        </div>
    </section>
</LayoutBase>
